-- A throw in `init` is a defect of the mount (docs/design/browser-direct.md
-- §8.2): `init` is a function every platform calls when the program mounts
-- (boundary.md §9.8.16), inside the program's mount, which `run` enters
-- through the dispatch guard, so the page stops and the development build
-- shows the crash screen — on `browser-direct` and on `browser-tea` alike,
-- one golden. (Until `init` was a function, `browser-tea` evaluated it
-- where `main` was, while the module loaded, and this page had a
-- `.tea-expected` of its own.) The release builds of both show no screen
-- (`InitThrows.release-expected`).
import Html exposing (Html)
import Tea


view : String → Html {}
view _ = <p>never shown</p>


main : Tea.Program
main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → Debug.todo "init threw", update = λ_ m → m, view = view }
